G0 (algebra). Engine T5 (cfg361_pm.py / cfg366_pm.py / cfg372_pm.py):  extra = fsw * max(s_ph - s_c, 0).
   Two-regime rule: extra = 0 where s_c >= s_ph (cold regime: ordinary cold matter, phantom adds nothing);
                    extra = s_ph - s_c where s_c < s_ph (phantom regime, capped at rho_ph - rho_cold); times the bound switch f.
   => piecewise definition of max(0, s_ph - s_c) times f: term-for-term the same expression, same s_c (engine's CIC cell
      density x (1 - f_b)), same s_ph (baryon-only, unfiltered), same f. G0: IDENTICAL.
   CFG366's 'literal local min rule' (dark <= cold present, added on top of the Newtonian cold) adds 0 = S0: NOT this rule.
   CFG366/372 RES = this rule's e minus its catchment average: this rule is RES's R_c -> infinity limit (CFG366 C2a).

